# The real programs the ladder is climbed on, pinned the way sysroots/manifest pins a libc.
#
# Five columns, tab separated: the name, the version, the licence, the sha256 of the archive, and
# the URL. Lines starting with a hash are comments. This is a separate file from sysroots/manifest
# because these are not sysroots: nothing here ends up in a tree a compiler searches, and what they
# are for is being built against one. The columns are the same five so that the fetch is the same
# fetch, which is that nothing is downloaded without a hash and nothing is downloaded from a URL
# that is not written down here.
#
# sqlite is rung 1 of spec/14-target-ladder.md in tamnd/rucc, and the version is the one that
# repository's own library check pins, so the two are asking about the same quarter of a million
# lines of somebody else's C rather than about two different ones.

